@7019 = ~Snow Leopard Charm~

@7020 = ~Shamans of many barbarian clans have long looked upon the snow leopard as one of the most graceful and swift hunters of the frozen lands. Many times, the warriors of these clans mimic the movements of the large, white cats during fierce combat. In addition, the barbarian shamans would sometimes create spells that would temporarily imbue the warriors with the dexterity of the snow leopards. However, since these spells were temporary, oftentimes the spell would wear off at inopportune times.

It is said, however, that a group of barbarian shamans once congregated deep within the Dales to find a way to better harness the swift agility of the snow leopard. For nearly a year, the shamans remained out of sight from their home clans, busily focusing their attentions on the magic of the snow leopard. Then one day, the shamans returned to their respective clans, each holding a small necklace made of silver, with a pendant that resembled a snow leopard's paw. The shamans gave this pendant to the strongest warrior of each clan. Once placed around the neck of the warrior, the dexterity of the snow leopard filled their powerful bodies. From then on, the Snow Leopard Charm, as it became known, became one of the most prized artifacts within barbarian clans. Only the mightiest warriors wore the amulet, and it became the goal of all young warriors to one day be adorned with the Snow Leopard Charm.

Over time, the legend of these pendants spread beyond the barbarian clans, catching the attention of thieves and treasure hunters across the Realms. Many such amulets have since disappeared, stolen from barbarian warriors by cunning rogues seeking to profit from their power. As a result, few Snow Leopard Charms remain in the possession of the clans.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Dexterity +2

Weight: 1~

@7021 = ~Improved Snow Leopard Charm~

@7022 = ~Improved Snow Leopard Charm

Shamans of many barbarian clans have long looked upon the snow leopard as one of the most graceful and swift hunters of the frozen lands. Many times, the warriors of these clans mimic the movements of the large, white cats during fierce combat. In addition, the barbarian shamans would sometimes create spells that would temporarily imbue the warriors with the dexterity of the snow leopards. However, since these spells were temporary, oftentimes the spell would wear off at inopportune times.

It is said, however, that a group of barbarian shamans once congregated deep within the Dales to find a way to better harness the swift agility of the snow leopard. For nearly a year, the shamans remained out of sight from their home clans, busily focusing their attentions on the magic of the snow leopard. Then one day, the shamans returned to their respective clans, each holding a small necklace made of silver, with a pendant that resembled a snow leopard's paw. The shamans gave this pendant to the strongest warrior of each clan. Once placed around the neck of the warrior, the dexterity of the snow leopard filled their powerful bodies. From then on, the Snow Leopard Charm, as it became known, became one of the most prized artifacts within barbarian clans. Only the mightiest warriors wore the amulet, and it became the goal of all young warriors to one day be adorned with the Snow Leopard Charm.

Over time, the legend of these pendants spread beyond the barbarian clans, catching the attention of thieves and treasure hunters across the Realms. Many such amulets have since disappeared, stolen from barbarian warriors by cunning rogues seeking to profit from their power. As a result, few Snow Leopard Charms remain in the possession of the clans.

By combining all powers of the original Snow Leopard Charm with Deep Red Ioun Stone and Amulet of Protection +1 Cromwell was able to enhance the item's magical abilities even more. The Lucky Coin of Tymora was attached and through the powers of the Permanency Scroll it grants its bonuses constantly.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- wearer is under permanent effect of Luck spell
- Dexterity +3
- Armor Class: +1
- Saving Throws: +1~

@7023 = ~Assassin's Dream +4~

@7024 = ~Assassin's Dream +4

Stories tell of daggers wielded by the most infamous thieves and assassins of the Realms, each imbued with a fragment of their wielder's cunning, precision, and malice. Over decades, these weapons absorbed the essence of their masters, carrying echoes of their infamous deeds.

With the help of the Manual of Elaboration, master craftsman was able to extract and weave their lingering magical auras into a single blade. The result is this dagger, a creation not of steel and shards but of pure essence. When held, the weapon seems to move with a will of its own, subtly guiding its owner's hand with the wisdom of long-dead assassins.

To wield this blade is to carry the weight of countless lives taken and to feel the shadows of its former masters at your side. It is said that those who hold it too long may find their own spirit overshadowed by the whispers of the past.

STATISTICS:
- Can only be wielded in main hand

Equipped abilities:
- Stealth Strike +40% when used as a single weapon or with a shield
- Immunity to Poison and Backstab

Special ability:
Assassination: Once per day

THAC0: +4 bonus
Damage: 1D6 +4
Damage type: piercing
Weight: 1
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: 1-handed
Require: 3 Strength~

@7025 = ~Girdle of Beatification~

@7026 = ~Girdle of Beatification
Priests of Helm in Berdusk consecrated this belt and gave it to the warrior Thom Wainwright, who had performed a number of great services for the church, including the destruction of the Unseeing Eye and the cult that followed him, the Blinded Acolytes. Thom wore the girdle proudly until he fell into severe debt in his later years. To his undying regret, he auctioned it off to a well-known priest of Mask.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- wearer is constantly under the effects of Bless and Protection from Evil spells

Weight: 2~

@7027 = ~Insulated Arcs of Disredain~

@7028 = ~Insulated Arcs of Disredain
Disredain was an eccentric wizard who became enthralled with the manipulation of electricity. In addition to the wands he created, Disredain made a number of experimental magic items during a fifteen-year period of frenzied research.  This belt was one of the items he did not think highly of. Consisting of large, crescent-shaped slices of mottled copper sitting back to back, the belt is quite thick and unique in appearance. A cleric of Talos named Ylkath wore the Arcs for three decades before he died of old age. His companion, the Umberlant priestess Ashalla of the Jade Tide, kept the belt for barely three years before she was shot dead by pirates that survived one of her nautical attacks. The pirates sold the belt to a fence. Its history past that point is unknown.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Electrical Damage: +10% bonus
- Electricity Resistance: +30%

Weight: 1~

@7029 = ~Cloverleaf~

@7030 = ~Cloverleaf
The halfling Tip Eldermaple was noted in his town for never losing at cards. The halfling attributed his good fortune to the blessings of Tyche and lived a long, quiet, and very prosperous life. 

When Tip finally died at the age of one hundred and three, he left his favorite belt to his son, who discovered that the belt buckle had caught a four-leaf clover in the clasp. Whether Tip had placed the clover there himself, or whether it had simply been stuck there after a tumble down a hill in his youth, no one will ever know. What is known is that Tip's fortune passed down to his son, until the belt was stolen from him by an ogre while he was traveling along the Sword Coast.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Luck
- 5% Magic Resistance

Weight: 2~

@7031 = ~Coin~

@7032 = ~Lucky Coin of Tymora~

@7033 = ~Coins are small, round pieces of precious metal, minted with intricate designs and symbols of their issuing authority. They are used as currency throughout the realms, valued for their material worth and utility in trade.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0~

@7034 = ~Lucky Coin of Tymora
This small, silver coin gleams faintly, as though touched by divine light. One side is engraved with a delicate four-leaf clover, symbolizing the favor of Tymora, the goddess of luck, while the other remains smooth and unadorned. Revered as a token of Tymora's unpredictable grace, this coin holds the power to invoke her blessing when tossed. However, as with all matters of luck, its effects are uncertain. A flip of the coin carries a 50% chance to grant Tymora's favor and a 50% chance to leave the outcome unchanged. Adventurers often treasure such coins as charms, relying on the goddess's capricious nature to aid them in dire moments.

STATISTICS:

Special abilities:
The coin can be tossed 3 times per day, if it lands on the side with clover engraving, it grants the effects of Luck spell as if cast by a 20th level Mage.

Weight: 0~

@7035 = ~Cloak of Mystra~

@7036 = ~Cloak of Mystra

Even though wizards can harbor powerful spells, their main weakness is the fact that they cannot wear any sort of armor without suffering severe limitations to their casting abilities. Although with proper training wizards may overcome these restrictions, wizards will normally choose to enchant their robes or a ring to have deflective properties so as to remain unfettered by bulky armor. But if by chance a talented fighter, or a skilled bowman connected with their weapon, the wizard would not have the fortitude to last long.

Clerics of Mystra, seeing this dilemma that fell upon the wizards of the land, made cloaks blessed by Mystra herself. These cloaks granted the wizard special damage resistances where some damage that was dealt out from a weapon would be negated. Needless to say that wizards who acquired the cloaks, which eventually were called Mystra's Blessing, felt even more powerful, if not invulnerable, which often led them to reckless decisions.

The item seems to be attuned to the Mage who wore it before it got into your hands and it rejects any attempts at putting it on. Maybe some craftsman would know how to make the item usable once again?

STATISTICS:

Special:
- can only be worn by a Mage attuned to the item

Equipped ability:

+20% Resistance to damage taken from all weapon types.

Weight: 3~

@7037 = ~Cloak of Mystra

Even though wizards can harbor powerful spells, their main weakness is the fact that they cannot wear any sort of armor without suffering severe limitations to their casting abilities. Although with proper training wizards may overcome these restrictions, wizards will normally choose to enchant their robes or a ring to have deflective properties so as to remain unfettered by bulky armor. But if by chance a talented fighter, or a skilled bowman connected with their weapon, the wizard would not have the fortitude to last long.

Clerics of Mystra, seeing this dilemma that fell upon the wizards of the land, made cloaks blessed by Mystra herself. These cloaks granted the wizard special damage resistances where some damage that was dealt out from a weapon would be negated. Needless to say that wizards who acquired the cloaks, which eventually were called Mystra's Blessing, felt even more powerful, if not invulnerable, which often led them to reckless decisions.

Through the use of Manual of Elaboration, the item's been slightly improved and now it can be used by any Mage without the need to attune to it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped ability:

+20% Resistance to damage taken from all weapon types.

Weight: 3~

@7038 = ~This powerful elixir is similar to the potion of heroism in that it effectively raises the imbiber's level and can be used by all character classes. This affects Hit Points, THAC0, and thieving abilities, although it does not raise the backstab multiplier. This effect is applied to the base, before any attribute modifiers are added.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2
Hit Points: +20% temporary (base only)
Hide In Shadows: +20% (base only)
Pick Pockets: +20% (base only)
Open Locks: +20% (base only)
Find Traps: +20% (base only)
Duration: 4 turns

Weight: 1~

@7039 = ~This potion is imbued with a powerful enchantment that will simulate a temporary increase in level. The effect lasts for 2 hours, which makes this potion a powerful ally in a deadly combat. This potion may only be used by warriors.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: +10% (base only)
THAC0: +1
Duration: 2 hours

Weight: 1~

@7040 = ~Blightwood +5~

@7041 = ~Crafted from three distinct clubs, Blightwood +5 is a weapon that rewards patience and precision. Its enchantments make it especially effective when striking unnoticed, momentarily reducing an enemy's ability to fight back. While simple in form, those who underestimate its magic often regret it.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
- Applies cumulative -1 penalty to AC and thac0 for 2 rounds and reduces enemy crushing resistance by 2% for 1 round if the enemy is not immune to that damage type (no save)
- Critical hit chance increased by 5%
- Each critical hit performed with this weapon grants additional 3 crushing damage
- Wielder gains additional +2 thac0 at night or in dungeons

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d6+5 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Club
Type: One-handed
Requires:
5 Strength

Weight: 3~

@7042 = ~The cloak can be made in every possible shape with just about every type of fabric. The most common forms are a circular piece of fabric with a hole in the center for the head, and fabric draped from neck, connected by a chain, brooch, cord, or pins. Talented drow weavers have woven strands of adamantine into the cloak, thus rendering it useless if exposed to the light—the effect of which will turn the cloak to dust.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Hide In Shadows: +25%
– Save vs. Breath: +6

Weight: 3~

@7043 = ~This cloak belongs to Solaufein, the drow warrior. It increases the wearer's Hide In Shadows abilities. Talented drow weavers have woven strands of adamantine into this cloak, thus rendering it useless if exposed to the light—the effect of which will turn the cloak to dust.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Hide In Shadows: +25%
– Save vs. Breath: +6

Weight: 3~

@7044 = ~This green cloak resembles a normal cloak. Wearing it makes any person able to hide in shadows with astonishing ability. As per the Thief ability though, the moment the wearer attacks or otherwise makes his/her presence known, the wearer must leave the shadows.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Hide In Shadows: +10%

Weight: 3~

@7045 = ~Ring of Gaxx
This ring is relatively unadorned, but the vile magic within radiates intense evil. Indeed, its creator, Kangaxx, was no less evil himself, even before millennia of undeath honed his power. It is said that a cadre of Netheril mages fought and imprisoned the demilich once, but being unable to truly destroy him they became liches themselves to stand guard over his remains. The construction of the ring may have led to their enmity, as each of the gem's nine facets was supposedly empowered by sacrifice and death.

STATISTICS

Armor Class: +2 Bonus
Saving Throws: +2 Bonus
Magic Resistance: +10% Bonus
Special Abilities: Immunity to Poison
Equipped Abilities: Wearer regenerates 1 hit point every 3 seconds
Special Use:  Invisibility, once per day
                      Double movement speed and attacks per round for 10 seconds, three time per day~

@7046 = ~Improved Ring of Gaxx
This ring is relatively unadorned, but the vile magic within radiates intense evil. Indeed, its creator, Kangaxx, was no less evil himself, even before millennia of undeath honed his power. It is said that a cadre of Netheril mages fought and imprisoned the demilich once, but being unable to truly destroy him they became liches themselves to stand guard over his remains. The construction of the ring may have led to their enmity, as each of the gem's nine facets was supposedly empowered by sacrifice and death.

The Ring has recently been combined with a powerful Ring of Protection +3 and a Ring of Regeneration. The result has surely been worth the attempt.

STATISTICS

Armor Class: +3 Bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Saving Throws: +3 Bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Magic Resistance: +20% Bonus
Special Abilities: Immunity to Poison
Equipped Abilities: Wearer regenerates 1 hit point every 2 seconds

Special Use: Invisibility, once per day

Double movement speed and attacks per round for 10 seconds, three time per day~

@7047 = ~Knight Wesic of the Most Noble Order of the Radiant Heart often said, "Attack swiftly and your enemy will be so overwhelmed that the battle will be yours." He lived this principle through these bracers. Before engaging in righteous battle, he would unlock the magic of the Blinding Strike and quickly rush at his enemy. More often than not, his opponent would fall within the first few seconds of battle.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Double movement speed and attacks per round for 12 seconds once per day~

@7048 = ~Stained in Blood +6

A meticulous application of blood taken from several powerful creatures has given this armor a fearful look and imbued it with bizarre magical abilities.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class: -1 (-3 vs. slashing, 1 vs. crushing)
Equipped Ability: +50% Resistance to Fire

Special abilities:
- War Paint: enemies that hit the wearer suffer non-cumulative 15% loss to the amount of physical damage that they deal for 2 rounds
- Blood Rage:
    wearer gains +3 to THAC0, +3 to damage, +2 to Strength, immunity to Fear, +4 bonus to Critical Chance and his number of attacks per round is doubled for 1 turn
    wearer cannot become enraged while under the effect of the spell
    while under the effect of the spell, the warrior suffers a +5 penalty to AC and loses awareness of the damage he receives (The Hit Points are masked for the duration of the spell)

Weight: 7
Requires: 8 Strength~

@7049 = ~Boots of The Ranger Lord

The exact origin of these boots is not known even to the wisest sages. Some believe that it is a relic with divine origin, but the majority of sages say that the boots are most probably made by Dryads or Swanmays or some other woodland beings in return of a great service a high level ranger had done. The boots are made of light but strongly enchanted leaves. Reforging the boots using a Permanency Scroll on the combination of the Boots of The Woodland, two pairs of Boots of Speed and three scrolls of Improved Haste, they can now make the wearer swing more often even when not hasted.

STATISTICS

Equipped Abilities:
– Permanent Haste
– +1/2 extra attack per round~

@7050 = ~Improved Boots of The Ranger Lord

The exact origin of these boots is not known even to the wisest sages. Some believe that it is a relic with divine origin, but the majority of sages say that the boots are most probably made by Dryads or Swanmays or some other woodland beings in return of a great service a high level ranger had done. The boots are made of light but strongly enchanted leaves. The boots were once reforged and changed to Boots of The Ranger Lord. Now they are improved again to reach their ultimate power. An incident which can even confirm the opinion of those who believe that such fantastic boots must have a divine element involved.

STATISTICS

Equipped Abilities:

Permanent Haste
+1/2 extra attack per round
Dexterity: +3 bonus
Armor Class: +7 bonus vs. missiles

Requires: 15 Dexterity~

@7051 = ~Elven Ancient Expertise

This extraordinary potion reveals the secrets and ancient knowledge of elves.

STATISTICS:

Grants 250,000 permanent experience points per each class of the imbiber.~

