@7062 = ~Combined with the Serpent Shaft, this dark halberd has the ability to slay an opponent with a single blow—unless they can survive the sudden loss of their head.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Cloak of Fear three times per day
  Special: Affected enemies flee in terror for 4 rounds (Save vs. Spell negates)
  Range: 0
  Duration: Instant
  Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius

Combat abilities:
– Hit target must save vs. Poison or suffer 3d6 points of poison damage
– 10% chance of decapitating opponent with each successful attack (unless the target saves vs. Death with a -2 penalty)

THAC0: +6
Damage: 1d10+6 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Halberd
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 13 Strength

Weight: 10~

@7063 = ~Atonement involves making reparations, paying a price. The Cloak of Atonement takes this requirement literally. In exchange for protection and safety, it will leech the health of its wearer to power itself.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities (up to 5 charges each):
– instant cast of Armor of Faith and Chant at level 15 on self
  constitution score reduced by 2 points for 8 hours

- instant cast of Death Ward and Chaotic Commands at level 15 on self
  constitution score reduced by 3 points for 8 hours
  
- instant cast of Shield of Archons on self
  constitution score reduced by 4 points for 8 hours

The item does not disappear, when all of its charges are used.

Weight: 3~

@7064 = ~Assassin's Dream +5~

@7065 = ~Assassin's Dream +5

Stories tell of daggers wielded by the most infamous thieves and assassins of the Realms, each imbued with a fragment of their wielder's cunning, precision, and malice. Over decades, these weapons absorbed the essence of their masters, carrying echoes of their infamous deeds.

With the help of the Manual of Elaboration, master craftsman was able to extract and weave their lingering magical auras into a single blade. The result is this dagger, a creation not of steel and shards but of pure essence. When held, the weapon seems to move with a will of its own, subtly guiding its owner's hand with the wisdom of long-dead assassins.

To wield this blade is to carry the weight of countless lives taken and to feel the shadows of its former masters at your side. It is said that those who hold it too long may find their own spirit overshadowed by the whispers of the past.

The already powerful Assassin's Dream +4 has been upgraded to this fabulous weapon, which is undoubtedly the most fearsome blade in hands of a thief or an assassin.

STATISTICS:
- Can only be wielded in main hand

Equipped abilities:
- Stealth Strike +50% when used as a single weapon or with a shield
- +1 Attack per round, when used as a single weapon or with a shield
- Immunity to Poison and Backstab
- 5% on any hit to turn the wielder invisible for 1-turn.

Special ability:
Assassination: Twice per day

THAC0: +5 bonus
Damage: 2D4 +5
Damage type: piercing
Weight: 1
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: 1-handed
Require: 3 Strength~

@7066 = ~Bracers of Brute Force~

@7067 = ~Bracers of Brute Force
Though deceptively elegant in design, these heavy metal wristbands are etched with ancient sigils of war and rage. Worn by a long-forgotten duelist who favored brute strength over finesse, they channel raw power into each blow. However, their unbalanced weight and aggressive enchantment throw off the wearer's aim, making precision strikes more difficult.

STATISTICS:

+2 bonus to melee damage
–2 penalty to THAC0

Weight: 2~

@7068 = ~These gauntlets assist in the stalking and killing of prey. Favored by hunters of all kinds, they display their full power when donned by a Stalker. Made of supple leather with brass-buckled straps along the side, these gauntlets are often decorated with embroidered figures of stags, foxes, or, as is the case with this pair, wolves.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Dexterity: +1
– Hide in Shadows: +10%
– Stealth Strike: +10% (Stalkers only)

Weight: 2~

@7069 = ~Stalker Gauntlets~

@7070 = ~Ring of Vitality~

@7071 = ~Often bestowed upon seasoned adventurers by grateful temples, these golden rings are engraved with runes of endurance. Though not uncommon, each carries a quiet blessing that reinforces the body and fortifies the spirit.
STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
+20 Max HP~

@7072 = ~~

@7073 = ~~

@7074 = ~~

@7075 = ~~

@7074 = ~Soul Cleaver~

@7075 = ~Forged from the lifeless metal of the Abyss and quenched in the blood of a thousand souls, this blade hums with the same hateful resonance as its master's Wand. On the Prime Material Plane, where Orcus's demonic essence is muted, he channels his power through Soul Cleaver and each swing drains the will and vitality of those it strikes. Mortal flesh recoils not only from its edge, but from the hopeless certainty it carries — that all life must eventually serve the Lord of Undeath.

No mortal can wield it without being consumed by its power, yet its craftsmanship and dark enchantments make it an object of immense value to collectors and scholars of the forbidden.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
- 20% chance to cumulatively doom the target without saving throw for 5 rounds
- 50% chance to cumulatively reduce thte target's maximum HP by 10 for 5 rounds
- permanent effect of Greater Deathblow
- 30% chance to remove all instances of Stoneskin effect
- 50% chance to deal additional 4d4 poison damage (save vs death at -4 to avoid)

THAC0: +5
Damage: 2d8+5 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Two handed sword
Type: 2-handed
Requires:
 25 Strength

Weight: 50~

@7076 = ~In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service, these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon forth a 5th-level berserk warrior who will fight for the summoner for 3 turns. The horn may be used once per day.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Summon 5th-level warrior once per day
  Duration: 3 turns

Weight: 1~

@7077 = ~In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service, these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon forth a 7th-level berserk warrior who will fight for the summoner for 3 turns. The horn may be used once per day.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Summon 7th-level warrior once per day
  Duration: 3 turns

Weight: 1~

@7078 = ~In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service, these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon forth a 9th-level berserk warrior who will fight for the summoner for 3 turns. The horn may be used once per day.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Summon 9th-level warrior once per day
  Duration: 3 turns

Weight: 1~

@7079 = ~Amber Horn of Valhalla

In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon an improved hasted fifteenth level berserker warrior for 30 rounds. The warrior has 50% resistance to all damage types and 90% resistance to electricity. The horn may be used once per day.

Not Usable By:
 Wizard Slayer~

@7080 = ~Reinforced Horn of Valhalla

In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon an improved hasted eighteenth level berserker warrior for 30 rounds. The warrior has 70% resistance to all damage types and 95% resistance to electricity. The warrior will not be considered a summoned creature and thus won't be affected by spells such as Death Fog and Death Spell. The horn may be used once per day.

Not Usable By:
 Wizard Slayer~

@7081 = ~Ultimate Horn of Valhalla

In the halls of Valhalla rest the most valiant of warriors. Their service to war during their lives has rewarded them with honored positions in Valhalla. As part of their service these warriors must offer their service to any who blow a horn of Valhalla. This horn will summon an improved hasted 21st level berserker warrior for 30 rounds. The warrior has 75% resistance to all damage types and 100% resistance to electricity. The warrior will not be considered a summoned creature and thus won't be affected by spells such as Death Fog and Death Spell. The horn may be used once per day~

@7082 = ~These soft boots make the wearer move as silently as the woodland elves. Thieves love to get their hands on these boots, but the elves are reluctant about exporting them, fearful that they may be used for illegal purposes.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities :
– Hide in Shadows: +15%

Weight: 3~

@7083 = ~Silent Gale Treads~

@7084 = ~These boots are the work of a true master of leather-craft - someone who understands how enchantments cling to hide and cloth the way grain runs in wood.
By carefully unstitching and re-layering a cloak of stealth and three distinct sets of enchanted boots, the artificer has bonded those magicks into a single integrated design.

The result is a pair of impossibly light boots that shift air around each step, letting the wearer move with startling quiet and surprising swiftness.

STATISTICS:
Equipped abilities:
- Hide in Shadows: +25%
- Stealth Strike: +5%
- Permanent Haste effect

Weight: 0~

@7085 = ~Ring of Enduring Heart~

@7086 = ~Likely crafted only for champions who have risked all in service of the greater good, these rings are said to hold long, steady blessings.
Whatever journey brought this one into the demon's keeping must have been gruesome, although the item's enchantments do not seem to be corrupted.

STATISTICS:
Equipped abilities:
- +30 Max HP
- Regenerate 1 Hit Point per round~

@7087 = ~Cloak of the Second Strike~

@7088 = ~This dark, close-cut cloak is sewn from overlapping panels of shadow-silk that shift with every motion of the wearer. It was commissioned for the most accomplished burglars of Athkatla, where a heartbeat often separates success from a blade in the back. When worn by one trained to rely on speed rather than brute strength, the cloak urges the body forward into a second motion before the first has fully ended.

STATISTICS:
Equipped abilities:
- +1/2 extra attack per round~

@7089 = ~The delicate yet sturdy craftsmanship of the elven races allows them to design many beautiful yet utilitarian goods. Among these is elven chain mail, which is so finely wrought that it can be worn under normal clothing without revealing its presence. This and its lightness allows it to be worn by Thieves and Fighter/Mages with few restrictions.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 5 (3 vs. slashing, 7 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 7~

@7090 = ~Woven by the finest of elven craftsmen, this mail feels more akin to cloth than to metal. The armor may be worn by Thieves with few penalties and by Fighter/Mages without removing their spellcasting ability.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 4 (2 vs. slashing, 6 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 8~

@7091 = ~This light but strong mail is of sylvan elf construction, and therefore its elegance is only exceeded by its rarity. Normally granted only to especially brave elves, seldom is this armor be found outside of a wood elf tribe, and rarer still on someone not of elven lineage.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 3 (1 vs. slashing, 5 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 10~

@7092 = ~The Bards of Melody were a small band of half-elf bardic warriors who entertained and defended scattered elven communities throughout Calimshan. Enchantments allowed only minstrels to wear their armor, the magical links sliding together to produce beautiful melodies as they danced or fought. Unfortunately, the Bards of Melody were disbanded hundreds of years ago, and the secret of "playing" the armor faded with them.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 2 (0 vs. slashing, 4 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 12~

@7093 = ~The lore of this suit is difficult to determine, either due to the exotic circumstances from which it sprang or the wish of its previous owner to conceal its location. Secrecy would certainly be desirable, as even rumors of such a mail as this could provoke deadly interest. It is the pinnacle of elven craft and a truly blessed item.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 1 (-1 vs. slashing, 3 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 15~

@7094 = ~While in exile from Myth Drannor, Aslyferund learned the secret of fashioning powerful elven armor by gilding and heavily enchanting normal elven chain. Alas, his refusal to divulge the secret lead to his murder by a rival smith.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Immunity to normal weapons
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 0 (-2 vs. slashing, 2 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 15~

@7095 = ~Woven by the finest of elven craftsmen, this mail feels more akin to cloth than to metal. The armor may be worn by Thieves with few penalties and by Fighter/Mages without removing their spellcasting ability.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 4 (2 vs. slashing, 6 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 8~

@7096 = ~Hide armor is made from the thick hide of a very large animal (an elephant for example) or from many layers of normal leather from common animals, like cows. Hide armor is far too bulky, inflexible and heavy to be used much in advanced human cultures. However, among the barbaric humanoid masses throughout the dark forests and misty jungles of the world, hide armor is common. Even though it does offer more protection than leather armor, one must get by the offensive odor and shoddy appearance in order to wear it effectively. Even though Thieves can wear this armor, it has a negative effect on their abilities.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Open Locks: -10%
– Find Traps: -10%
– Pick Pockets: -10%
– Stealth Strike: -20%

Armor Class: 6 (8 vs. piercing and missile)
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 40~

@7097 = ~The delicate yet sturdy craftsmanship of the elven races allows them to design many beautiful yet utilitarian goods. Among these is elven chain mail, which is so finely wrought that it can be worn under normal clothing without revealing its presence. This and its lightness allows it to be worn by Thieves and Fighter/Mages with few restrictions.

This item, like most drow equipment, is created using adamantine, an alloy of adamantite that quickly turns to dust if removed from the Underdark.

This magical drow chain mail gives the wearer a bonus of 5% to Magic Resistance and takes 1 off of the Speed Factor of all spells cast by the wearer of the armor.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Magic Resistance: +5%
– Improves casting time by 1
– Open Locks: -5%
– Find Traps: -5%
– Pick Pockets: -20%
– Stealth Strike: -10%
– Spellcasting is not disabled

Armor Class: 2 (0 vs. slashing, 4 vs. crushing)
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 12~

@7098 = ~The sturdy craftsmanship of the drow allows them to design many beautiful yet utilitarian goods. Among these is drow chain mail, which is so finely wrought that it can be worn under normal clothing without revealing its presence. This and its lightness allows it to be worn by Thieves and Fighter/Mages with few restrictions.

This item, like most drow equipment, is created using adamantine, an alloy of adamantite that quickly turns to dust if removed from the Underdark.

