Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 10~

@7103 = ~Ring of Clumsiness: The Jester's Folly
The most notorious owner of this ring made a substantial living exploiting its cursed nature. Gregoria the Foole, a Jester by trade, would use his incomparable sleight of hand to switch this ring with that of a patsy taken from his audience. The rest of his performance would involve the mocking of the newly clumsy individual, much to the delight of their comrades. The ring was removed (by a method known only to the wily Jester) only once the stooge had promised no reprisals for the treatment he had received, though Gregoria frequently still had to make a hasty retreat. His last known performance was rumored to have been an ill-humored mage in Zhentil Keep: a show from which he did not flee quite fast enough.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Dexterity: -50%
– Stealth Strike: -50%
– 75% chance of spellcasting failure
– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell


@7105 = ~Master of the High Forest

When younger, Cernd spent a cycle of seasons meditating on his role within nature.  He made no shelter, wanting to feel the land unhindered.  Nature may have appreciated the intent, she also knows that, for all their dedication, at times her children can be foolish. Cernd found this cloak before the cold season set in, seemingly woven to fit him from the very undergrowth.  The message was clear: he can appreciate the rain while still seeking shelter from it. Only Cernd may use this cloak.

The cloak has been upgraded to a very mighty protective shelter and now it also grants additional daily spells to Cernd.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Saving Throw: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks

Equipped abilities:

Magic Resistance: +25%
Cernd can memorize one additional 6th and one additional 7th level spells.

Weight:  3

Usable By:
 Cernd~

@7106 = ~This beautiful cloak is made from the pelt of a yeti. The cloak was sewn by master Maheer in Athkatla, and it retains some of the natural resistances inherent to yeti. Further enhanced by Cromwell, the garment now provides better protection.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +2 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Saving Throw: +2 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Cold Resistance: +50%

Weight: 1~

@7107 = ~Cloak of Arcane Immortality

As the result of the combination of three powerful cloaks, this magical item is probably the ultimate possible cloak for any character who qualifies the requirements to wear it.

Equipped Abilities:

- Armor Class: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Saving Throw: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Regeneration: 3 hit points per round
- Max HP Bonus: +15

Requirements: 18 Wisdom and Intelligence

Usable by:
 Good aligned Necromancers~

@7108 = ~Cloak of the Daywalker

With the help of Adamantite Dust to absorb the magical aura from Dragomir's Cloak and an additional Cloak of Protection, Dragomir’s Cloak has reached its full potential.

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +2 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Saving Throw: +2 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
- Constitution: +2
- Increases attacks per round by 1/2

Allows a vampire to travel outside during the day and in full view of the sun.~

@7109 = ~This artefact was presented to you by Helm's messenger as a token of gratitude for your bravery and willingness to confront Demogorgon, the prince of demons. The apparition claimed the present to be a powerful ward blessed by The Watcher himself.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class: +4 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Saving Throws: +4 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks

Not Usable By:
 Wizard Slayer~

@7110 = ~De'Arnise Signet Ring (Enhanced)

This ring was given to Nalia by her father upon her ascension to adulthood. Bonded to her blood as it is, the ring's powers cannot be used by anyone else.

After enhancements the ring has the following statistics:

Armor Class: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Saving Throw: +3 bonus, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
Fire resistance: +90%
Nalia can memorize two additional spells per spell level.

Usable By:
 Nalia~

@7111 = ~Enhanced Cloak of Dragomir

The Cloak of Dragomir and Cloak of the Dead have been combined and lined with a Cloak of Protection, and the resulting combination, though imperfect, enables Hexxat to move much more freely during the day.

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
– Saving Throws: +1, that stacks with simiar bonuses from rings and cloaks
– Constitution: +1
– Increases attacks per round by 1/2

Allows a vampire to travel outside during the day and in full view of the sun, albeit with the following penalties:
– Strength: -1
– Dexterity: -1
– Intelligence: -1
– Wisdom: -1
– Charisma: -1~

@7112 = ~Barbarian's Dream

This outstanding chain mail is the final result of combining four powerful chain armors. It was further reinforced with amber by the artificer Lady Elowen.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Fire Resistance: +20%
- Resistance to Electricity: +40%
- Resistance to damage from all weapon types: +10%

Armor Class: -2
Weight: 7
Requires: 8 Strength~

@7113 = ~Reinforced Full Plate +5

Full plate armor is the best armor a warrior can buy, both in appearance and protection. The Full Plate +2 was merged with the Improved Ankheg Plate Mail, and further reinforced with amber by the artificer Lady Elowen.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Resistance to Acid, Cold and Fire: +25%
- Resitance to Electricity: +65%
- Regeneration: 1HP per second

Armor Class: -4
Weight: 40
Requires: 15 Strength~

@7114 = ~Boots of The Riskbreaker Lord

Legends say that Hermes himself had made these boots and bestowed them on one of his mortal followers. Along with the gift came a promise that the boots may be improved once the follower's Riskbreaker strength has grown, something which apparently had never happened.

The Artificer Lady Elowen fulfilled the original promise by elevating the legendary boots to their true potential.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Bonus to Movement Speed: +4
- Armor Class Bonus: +4
- Bonus to all Saving Throws: +4
- APR bonus: +1/2
- Regeneration: 1 HP per second
- Magic Damage Resistance: +25%
- Immunity to the 3rd level Haste and Slow spells (including Golem Slow)

Usable By:
 Riskbreaker~

@7115 = ~Reinforced Amber Ioun Stone

This headwear is strengthened with reinforced amber and wrapped in a protective outer shell, made of amber as well.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class bonus: +2
- Resistance to Electricity: +15%
- +20 Max HP
- Mental Agility: +1 bonus to casting speed

Special: Protects against critical hits

Usable By:
 Cleric
 Druid~

@7116 = ~Shield of The Missionnaire +6

According to Lady Elowen, a story of a shield once belonged to a human cleric inspired her to create this piece. The clergyman was sent to the northern barbarian tribes as a messenger. Rumors say that his last words before death were: "I wish I was half as tough as they are".

An extra coating has been added to make the shield a bit more resilient.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Armor Class Bonus: +7
- Resistance to Elemental Damage: +20%
